# spun.cat holds als001, and mame-alias.sh has moved @ALIAS@ to als002 in the
# database. .spun get by the alias now gets als002, which is not installed,
# so it offers als002's suggested directory; y installs it. Then .spun get of
# an alias that names no app, through gui-test.py's proxy (@PORT@), ends with
# an error. ON ERROR (tokens $90 $8F, see spun-error.scn.in) traps it, which
# keeps the autoexec running but also keeps BASIC from printing the report,
# so the screen shows "Opening" and no app title. mame-alias.sh checks the
# proxy's log for the server's NoApp_ERROR, and mame.log for the trap (BASIC
# at $0000 on the line of the second get) and for no machine reset.
put @SPUN@ /dot/SPUN
put @CAT@ /sys/spun.cat
autostart .spun get @ALIAS@
autostart \x90\x8fFOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
autostart .spun -p @PORT@ get nosuchalias
autostart FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
seconds 35
key 16 y
snap 15 20 26 34
screen 34 Alias Test B
screen 34 Install to C:/apps/alsb? (y/n) y
